---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import { experience, education } from '../data/experience';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Anthony Maiorana is a PhD chemist with experience in industrial materials, product development, medical-device review, and independent scientific writing.">
  <PageIntro eyebrow="About / Anthony Maiorana" title="A few ways of looking at a problem." description="I’ve worked with molecules, manufacturing lines, and medical devices. Those experiences have made me interested in the space between a promising idea and something that works in the world."><div class="hero-links"><a class="button" href="/cv/">View my CV <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a><a class="text-link" href="/publications/">Publications & patents <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="arrow-icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" fill="none"><path d="M4 16 16 4M4 4h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></span></a></div></PageIntro>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="section content-grid"><div><p class="sidebar-label">What I bring to the question</p></div><div>
      <div class="capability"><h3>Connect the technical details.</h3><p>A material’s structure matters. So do the manufacturing process, the performance requirements, and the person who will use it. I’m comfortable moving between those levels of a problem.</p></div>
      <div class="capability"><h3>Work with incomplete evidence.</h3><p>Scientific and regulatory decisions rarely arrive with every uncertainty resolved. My work involves evaluating what the evidence supports, identifying what is missing, and deciding which questions matter most.</p></div>
      <div class="capability"><h3>Make complex work understandable.</h3><p>Through The Polymerist, I write about the relationships between chemistry, industrial capability, and commercial outcomes. The aim is to give readers enough context to ask better questions of their own.</p></div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Professional work</p><h2>Experience, in context.</h2></div></div>{experience.map(job => <article class="experience-item"><p class="dates">{job.dates}<br />{job.area}</p><div><h3>{job.organization}</h3><p class="role">{job.role}</p><ul>{job.details.map(detail => <li>{detail}</li>)}</ul></div></article>)}</section>
    <section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">Education & research</p><div class="education-grid">{education.map(item => <div><p class="meta">{item.year}</p><h3>{item.degree}</h3><p><strong>{item.institution}</strong></p><p>{item.detail}</p></div>)}</div></section>
    <section class="section content-grid"><p class="eyebrow">Outside a job description</p><div class="prose"><h2>Room to keep learning.</h2><p>The Polymerist is where I follow questions about the chemical industry. This website gives me a place to follow some of the others: how AI changes practical work, what makes a scientific discovery useful, and what I can learn by building tools myself.</p><p>I live in Washington, DC. Most people call me Tony. My scientific publications appear under Anthony Maiorana.</p></div></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
